Hit the same `MIR lowering '<Type>_message': UnresolvedVariable` symptom during unrelated codegen work, but this repro has **no name collision** — the failing method belongs to stdlib `IoError`, which the program never mentions. So whatever fix lands here needs to cover more than user↔stdlib short-name clashes; a spurious-reachability path pulls in `IoError.message` and then fails to lower it.

Minimal repro (native only; `--interp` runs fine):

```rask
struct Big { a: i64, b: i64, c: i64 }
enum LoadError { Missing }
extend LoadError {
    func message(self) -> string {
        match self { LoadError.Missing => return "x" }
    }
